the u.s will send another 270 million  dollars in military aid to help ukraine  in its five-month battle with russia the  white house says this will include drone  support consideration is being given to  possibly send fighter aircraft as well  this comes as russia and ukraine managed  to find common ground friday signing two  separate agreements to allow ukraine to  resume shipments of grain across the  black sea as russia lifts its naval  blockade but this morning russian  missiles are reportedly striking the key  port city of odessa holly williams has  the latest from  excuse me dunny pro in central ukraine  holly good morning  good morning well russia's been accused  of using hunger as a weapon of war by  blockading ukraine's ports contributing  to a dangerous spike in food prices  around the world now this new deal could  avert a global food crisis but it's  fragile and now less than a day later  ukraine says one of its ports has been  hit with cruise missiles calling it a  spit in the face to the u.n secretary  general  the russians and ukrainians refused to  sit at the same table and avoided  shaking hands but this deal could hold  off disaster in some of the world's  poorest countries it will bring relief  for developing countries on the edge of  bankruptcy and the most vulnerable  people on the edge of famine  more than 20 million tons of grain have  been stuck in ukraine and the war has  destroyed silos and crops contributing  to a surge in food prices the united  nations says 345  million people many in africa are now  marching to the brink of starvation  before the invasion ukraine was one of  the world's biggest exporters of grain  the breadbasket of europe  russia's blockade has been called a war  crime by the european union  though russia denies its weaponized  hunger  this however is irrefutable the deadly  violence unleashed by vladimir putin's  invasion  on thursday this woman lost her husband  when a crowded market was hit by  shelling but much-needed weapons are  arriving from the u.s and its allies  and they're making a difference  this week the u.s promised more highmar  rocket systems with a 50-mile range  they're game-changing according to  ukraine the ukrainians are making the  russians pay for every inch of territory  that they gain the u.s says russian  forces have only advanced six to 10  miles in eastern ukraine in the last 90  days these tactical gains have come at  an incredible cost  in terms of russian casualties and  destroyed equipment  ukraine's president vladimir zelansky  said in an interview this past week that  back in may and june his military was  losing up to 200 soldiers every day and  that's now down to 30. meanwhile the  head of britain's foreign intelligence  service predicts that russia's assault  is about to quote run out of steam after  some epic fails  jeff holly thank you very much
 

